WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome. Welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.569
You're here. You made it.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:04.904
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:07.807
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.376
Well, guys, the weather
right now is crazy.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.312
A state of emergency has been
declared here in New York

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:16.850
as a massive nor'easter slams
the East Coast with heavy rain,

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.119
flooding, and intense winds.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:21.120
Yep, we're in
a state of emergency,

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.922
or as Facebook calls it,
"Tuesday."

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.624
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:25.992
Seriously, it's gross out there.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:29.128
Right now, the entire East Coast
smells like damp mask.

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:34.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.370
Yeah, we're dealing with
that intense wind where

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.306
your mask blows off your face
and lands onto someone else's.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.974
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:43.676
Wait, I'm vaxxed.
Are you vaxxed?

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.111
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.046
Here in New York City,
the streets were so flooded,

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.516
all the shrimp at Bubba Gump
made a break for the Hudson.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.250
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.286
Let's go, boys! Yeah.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.454
That's right. Already,
thousands have lost power,

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.423
making it the one time
people actually turned on

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.192
their iPhone flashlights
on purpose.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.227
It's like,
"Oh, that's what it's for."

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.428
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:03.829
Let's get to some news.

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:06.131
Of course, everyone's been
talking about Facebook lately,

00:01:06.131 --> 00:01:08.801
and Mark Zuckerberg just
announced that he's "retooling"

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:11.303
the social-media platform
towards young adults

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:13.439
and away from older users.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:15.942
Honestly, just make it
a little harder to sign in

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.843
and you'll never see
an old person on Facebook again.

00:01:17.843 --> 00:01:19.745
[ Laughter ]
That's all you got to do.

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:24.116
[ Applause ]
"How many stop signs?

00:01:24.116 --> 00:01:27.754
Scan my face?"

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.622
My aunt's gonna
have a lot of free time.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.557
She can't use Facebook
to write "love this"

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:33.926
under every inspirational quote.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:36.596
You're really inspired today.
Wow.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:40.066
Meanwhile, today executives from
TikTok and Snapchat testified

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.168
before a Senate panel
for the first time.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.737
Usually, the only tick-tock
on Capitol Hill

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.673
is coming from
a senator's pacemaker.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.507
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:50.109
"It's not ticking anymore.
You better --"

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:51.444
[ Laughter ]
Give it a little --

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.346
There, now it's working again.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.347
Yeah, it was hours of
tech executives

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:57.450
trying to explain their apps
to senators.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.653
Experts are calling it a preview
of your family at Thanksgiving.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.788
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.790
"So how do I get
to the Snapchat?"

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.225
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:07.927
Yep, senators believe social
media is corrupting our teens,

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.228
and they might be
on to something,

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.264
because a bunch of 15-year-olds
barged in

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.132
for a "lick a senator"
challenge.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:16.201
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.201 --> 00:02:18.237
"Take his flag pin
then throw bologna at him."

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:21.907
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:23.342
That's a challenge.
-That's a challenge.

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:25.077
-Yeah, of course.
-Wet mask.

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:26.312
-Yeah. That's right.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.581
A TikTok executive appeared
before Senate.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:29.815
It was pretty interesting.

00:02:29.815 --> 00:02:31.817
Here's what happened
when they asked why TikTok

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:34.587
has so much misinformation
on its platform.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:37.890
♪ -Out to play ball
so we could ruin them ♪

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.426
♪ Mama said that it was okay ♪

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:43.395
♪ Mama said that
it was quite alright ♪

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:48.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.470
Some more news from Washington.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.304
President Biden
is still negotiating

00:02:52.304 --> 00:02:54.974
his new spending bill with
Congress and hopes to have

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.009
a deal by the end of this week.

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:59.546
Biden's bill
started at $3.5 trillion

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.480
and now it's down
to about $2 trillion.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.682
Right now he's like a guy
at the airport taking stuff

00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:05.618
out of his bag
to get it under 50 pounds.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:08.454
He's like, "I don't think
I need shirts, right?

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.456
How much are we going to
wear shirts, right?"

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.757
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:13.693
"I guess I could wear
my ski boots on the plane."

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.261
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.796
The deal is getting held up
'cause senators Joe Manchin

00:03:17.796 --> 00:03:20.833
and Kyrsten Sinema
keep adding stipulations.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:21.967
It's getting nuts.

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.235
Right now they won't
sign the bill

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:25.371
until Kyrie Irving
is allowed to play for the Nets.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:28.474
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.644
Some business news -- Hertz just
announced that it's buying

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:35.381
100,000 Teslas for its fleet of
rental cars.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.950
Yep. Then to give Hertz a taste
of their own medicine,

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.653
Tesla said, "Sorry, we don't
have any Teslas right now.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.688
Is a Kia Rio okay?"

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:46.158
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:50.129
Thank you.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.998
"That's all we have. Sorry.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.866
And with this rental,
you keep this car."

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.869
"It's your problem --
I mean, your car now."

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.237
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.206
Hey, I read about a man
in Georgia who's facing

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:03.943
federal charges
after he spent over $57,000

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:07.580
in COVID relief funds
on a single Pokemon card.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.947
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.947 --> 00:04:12.017
Wow. His wife would be
so embarrassed if she existed.

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:20.860
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.728
It's gonna be rough
when he gets to prison

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:24.563
and he explains he's there
because he loves Squirtle.

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:26.365
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:29.201
-Oh! Oh, oh!
-Hey, guys, get this.

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:32.204
I heard about a guy who bought
a Six Flags annual pass.

00:04:32.204 --> 00:04:33.373
How about this deal?

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:34.974
You get the Six Flags
annual pass, right?

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:37.977
It allows you to get
unlimited food for 150 bucks.

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:41.581
He's eaten nearly all of his
meals at Six Flags ever since.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.049
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:45.951
Of course, all the money
he saved is now going to doctors

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:47.854
to get his cholesterol
down from 1,000.

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.254
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.254 --> 00:04:51.857
And finally, a man in Lithuania
broke a world record

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:54.794
by sitting up to his neck
in a container of ice

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.061
for three hours.

00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:57.063
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:58.464
Then he stood up
and broke the record

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:00.366
for most disappointed
girlfriend.

